@lang en
-- Tests of ie-operation-and-construction.l4: ss 17, 18(b), (d), (e), (f), (g), 20(1), 21(2) and Schedule Part 2 "full age".
-- Expected values were read off the quoted text. Every boundary the text draws (22 December 1993, 14 January 1988, the day after the passing,
-- the commencement of this Act, the day a person attains full age) is tested on both sides and on the boundary itself.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`
IMPORT `ie-operation-and-construction`

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN expressed IS A DATE
      passed IS A DATE
      manner IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A BOOLEAN
      necessary IS A BOOLEAN
      restriction IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for section 17`
`facts for section 17` expressed passed manner power necessary restriction MEANS
    `Facts for section 17` WITH
        `the day on which the Act or provision is expressed to come into operation`   IS expressed
        `the day of the passing of the Act`                                            IS passed
        `the day on which it comes into operation is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner` IS manner
        `the Act confers a power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing for the purposes of the Act or provision`           IS power
        `the making or doing of it is necessary or expedient to enable the Act or provision to have full force and effect immediately on its coming into operation` IS necessary
        `a restriction imposed by the Act forbids doing it on the day in question`   IS restriction

§ `Section 17: the section applies only to a day subsequent to the date of the passing`

#ASSERT     `section 17 applies` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `section 17 applies` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 3 11) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17 applies` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 17 applies` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 3 9)  (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `Section 17(a): the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done at any time after the passing`

#ASSERT     `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 5 31) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 9)  `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- the day itself: no time of day is fixed for the passing
#ASSERT REFUSED `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "section 17 says \"after the passing\", and the Act fixes no time of day for the passing, so a thing on the same day is not answered"
-- the day is not to be fixed in a particular manner
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- "subject to any restriction imposed by the Act"
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- the section does not apply: the expressed day is not subsequent to the passing
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 3 9)  (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- a restriction is checked before the day is placed, so on the day of the passing it still answers FALSE and not a refusal
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§ `Section 17(b): a power necessary or expedient to give the Act full force on its commencement may be exercised at any time after the passing`

#ASSERT     `the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 9)  `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (a) and (b) are independent: a day fixed in a particular manner does not give a power under (b)
#ASSERT NOT `the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 11) `, the facts being` (`facts for section 17` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 18(b): gender`

#ASSERT `a word importing the` masculine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `passed or made on` (YMD 1900 1 1)
#ASSERT `a word importing the` masculine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `passed or made on` (YMD 1900 1 1)
#ASSERT `a word importing the` masculine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` `passed or made on` (YMD 1925 1 1)
-- feminine, in an Act: "passed on or after 22 December 1993"
#ASSERT NOT `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `passed or made on` (YMD 1993 12 21)
#ASSERT     `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `passed or made on` (YMD 1993 12 22)
#ASSERT     `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `passed or made on` (YMD 1993 12 23)
#ASSERT     `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `passed or made on` (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- feminine, in a statutory instrument: "made after that date"
#ASSERT NOT `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `passed or made on` (YMD 1993 12 21)
#ASSERT NOT `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `passed or made on` (YMD 1993 12 22)
#ASSERT     `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `passed or made on` (YMD 1993 12 23)
-- a Saorstat Eireann statute is an "Act", and was passed long before 1993
#ASSERT NOT `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` `passed or made on` (YMD 1925 1 1)

§ `Section 18(d): a reference to a child of a person includes an adopted child`

GIVEN passed IS A DATE
      after76 IS A BOOLEAN
      byPerson IS A BOOLEAN
      outside IS A BOOLEAN
      recognised IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about an adopted child`
`facts about an adopted child` passed after76 byPerson outside recognised MEANS
    `Facts about an adopted child` WITH
        `the day the Act was passed` IS passed
        `the Act was passed after the passing of the Adoption Act 1976` IS after76
        `the child was adopted by the person under the Adoption Acts 1952 to 1998 or another enactment to be construed together with them` IS byPerson
        `the child was adopted outside the State` IS outside
        `the adoption is recognised by virtue of the law for the time being in force in the State` IS recognised

-- limb (i): an Act passed after the passing of the Adoption Act 1976
#ASSERT     `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1980 1 1) TRUE  TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1980 1 1) FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1980 1 1) TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- limb (ii): an Act passed on or after 14 January 1988; a child adopted outside the State and recognised
#ASSERT NOT `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1988 1 13) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1988 1 14) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1988 1 15) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- outside the State but not recognised, or recognised but not adopted outside the State
#ASSERT NOT `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- limb (ii) also takes "a child to whom subparagraph (i) relates", so a child adopted by the person is included on or after 14 January 1988
#ASSERT     `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 2000 1 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1988 1 13) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- an Act passed before 14 January 1988 and after the 1976 Act still takes the child adopted by the person, by limb (i)
#ASSERT     `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 1988 1 13) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- no adoption at all
#ASSERT NOT `a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` (`facts about an adopted child` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 18(e): distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane (the height is ignored)`

GIVEN e IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Point
`the point` e n h MEANS
    Point WITH `east of the origin` IS e, `north of the origin` IS n, `above the origin` IS h

#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` 0 0 0) `and` (`the point` 3 4 0) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` 0 0 0) `and` (`the point` 3 4 100) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` 3 4 100) `and` (`the point` 0 0 0) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` 0 0 0) `and` (`the point` 0 0 100) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` 1 2 3) `and` (`the point` 1 2 3) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` 5 12 0) `and` (`the point` 0 0 7) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` (0 MINUS 3) (0 MINUS 4) 0) `and` (`the point` 0 0 0) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance between` (`the point` 10 10 0) `and` (`the point` 13 14 9) `within the meaning of section 18(e)` EQUALS 5

§ `Section 18(f): a consecutive series described by its first and last includes the first and the last`

#ASSERT     `the number` 5 `is a member of the series from` 5 `to` 9
#ASSERT     `the number` 9 `is a member of the series from` 5 `to` 9
#ASSERT     `the number` 7 `is a member of the series from` 5 `to` 9
#ASSERT NOT `the number` 4 `is a member of the series from` 5 `to` 9
#ASSERT NOT `the number` 10 `is a member of the series from` 5 `to` 9
#ASSERT     `the number` 5 `is a member of the series from` 5 `to` 5
#ASSERT NOT `the number` 6 `is a member of the series from` 5 `to` 5
#ASSERT `the number of members of the series from` 5 `to` 9 EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the number of members of the series from` 3 `to` 3 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of members of the series from` 1 `to` 2 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `the number of members of the series from` 9 `to` 5 BECAUSE "section 18(f) describes a series by its first and last members, and a last member that precedes the first does not describe one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the number` 7 `is a member of the series from` 9 `to` 5

§ `Section 18(g): marginal notes, shoulder notes, headings and cross-lines (subject to section 7)`

#ASSERT NOT `the matter is taken to be part of the enactment` `a marginal note placed at the side of a section or other provision`
#ASSERT NOT `the matter is taken to be part of the enactment` `a shoulder note placed at the beginning of a section or other provision`
#ASSERT NOT `the matter is taken to be part of the enactment` `a heading or cross-line of a Part, Chapter, section or other provision or group of provisions`
#ASSERT     `the matter is taken to be part of the enactment` `the text of a provision`
-- the text of a provision may always be construed
#ASSERT `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `the text of a provision` `a statutory instrument` FALSE FALSE
-- a note or heading may not be, unless section 7(1) lets a court use it
#ASSERT NOT `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `a marginal note placed at the side of a section or other provision` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT     `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `a marginal note placed at the side of a section or other provision` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT     `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `a shoulder note placed at the beginning of a section or other provision` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT     `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `a heading or cross-line of a Part, Chapter, section or other provision or group of provisions` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `a heading or cross-line of a Part, Chapter, section or other provision or group of provisions` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `a heading or cross-line of a Part, Chapter, section or other provision or group of provisions` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE TRUE
-- section 7 speaks of an Act, so it gives nothing for a statutory instrument
#ASSERT NOT `the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` `a marginal note placed at the side of a section or other provision` `a statutory instrument` TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 20(1): a definition or interpretation provision applies unless a contrary intention appears in the enactment or in the Act under which it is made`

#ASSERT     `the definition or interpretation provision is read as applicable` FALSE NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the definition or interpretation provision is read as applicable` TRUE  NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the definition or interpretation provision is read as applicable` FALSE (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT     `the definition or interpretation provision is read as applicable` FALSE (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the definition or interpretation provision is read as applicable` TRUE  (JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 21(2): Part 2 of the Schedule applies to an enactment that comes into operation AFTER the commencement of this Act (which is the end of 31 December 2005)`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      s IS A `What an enactment says about its own commencement`
      d IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment`
`an enactment of kind` k `that says` s `and was passed or made on` d MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS k
        `what it says about commencement`  IS s
        `the day of its passing or making` IS d

-- an Act expressed to come into operation on a particular day
#ASSERT     `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2006 1 2)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2005 11 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2006 1 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2005 11 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2005 12 31)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2005 11 1)))
#ASSERT     `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2030 1 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2029 1 1)))
-- an Act that says nothing: it comes into operation on the date of its passing (a day, no moment)
#ASSERT     `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2006 1 2)))
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2005 12 31)))
#ASSERT REFUSED `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2006 1 1))) BECAUSE "section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing, so whether an enactment that came into operation on 1 January 2006 did so after this Act is not answered"
-- a statutory instrument that says nothing: the end of the day before it is made
#ASSERT     `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2006 1 2)))
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2006 1 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2005 12 31)))
-- a statutory instrument expressed to come into operation on 1 January 2006: the same moment as this Act, so not after it
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2006 1 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2005 12 1)))
-- not answered while the commencement day is still to be fixed
#ASSERT REFUSED `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` `it is expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) BECAUSE "the particular day on which the enactment is to come into operation has not been fixed or ascertained"
-- this Act itself comes into operation at the same moment as itself, not after it
#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` `the facts about this Act`

§ `Schedule Part 2, "full age": the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event`

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      m IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts for full age`
`full age facts` a m MEANS
    `Facts for full age` WITH
        `the day on which the person attained the age of 18 years` IS a
        `the day on which the person married`                      IS m

-- attained 18 on 2024-05-01, not married
#ASSERT `the day on which the person attains full age` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2024 4 30) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT     `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2024 5 1)  `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT     `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2024 5 2)  `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is of full age throughout` (YMD 2024 4 30) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the person is of full age throughout` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) NOTHING) BECAUSE "the Act fixes no time of day at which a person attains full age, so whether the person was of full age throughout that day is not answered"
#ASSERT     `the person is of full age throughout` (YMD 2024 5 2) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) NOTHING)
-- married before attaining 18: "or sooner marries"
#ASSERT `the day on which the person attains full age` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2026 6 14) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)))
#ASSERT     `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2026 6 15) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)))
-- married after attaining 18: the earlier event decides, and "any time after either event"
#ASSERT `the day on which the person attains full age` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)
#ASSERT `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2030 1 1) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2024 5 1)) (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)))
-- married only (the 18th year not yet reached)
#ASSERT `the day on which the person attains full age` (`full age facts` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT     `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2026 6 15) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)))
-- the same day for both
#ASSERT `the day on which the person attains full age` (`full age facts` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)
-- neither event has happened
#ASSERT `the day on which the person attains full age` (`full age facts` NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the person is of full age at the end of` (YMD 2099 12 31) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is of full age throughout` (YMD 2099 12 31) `, the facts being` (`full age facts` NOTHING NOTHING)
